\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
1. What TLO Inventory does}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
TLO Inventory provides full inventory, incremental Add Shows processing, audio tagging, inventory searching, and artist-database searching. The source bundle contains the application sources and build utilities. The separate distribution ZIP contains native end-user applications for Windows, macOS, and generic Linux. The generic Linux applications are also used when running under WSL; there is no separate WSL application directory or WSL build.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
The full inventory function scans configured music roots, identifies core show metadata, prepares searchable setlist text, and builds the inventory output used by the included search tools.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Full Inventory scans configured music roots and rebuilds the inventory outputs.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Add Shows adds new content to an existing inventory without rerunning the full scan.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Standalone Tag and inventory-time Tag in Place write audio metadata when you choose to tag files. Tag Copy and Tag Copy/Delete Original are Full Inventory modes, not standalone Tagger functions.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- The included Search app searches the completed bootlist and setlist files after the distribution is extracted into TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
2. Installation package and TLOHome layout}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Each release has a source bundle and eight platform distribution ZIPs: complete and update packages for Windows onefile, Windows onedir, generic Linux, and macOS. Names follow TLO_V1.2Build351_complete_<platform>.zip and TLO_V1.2Build351_update_<platform>.zip. Use a complete package for a new installation. Use the matching update package only to refresh an existing TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The source bundle contains the current requirements DOCX, the current RTF user manual, application source, tests, and build utilities. Complete distributions include the current RTF user manual, FAQ, required databases, starter files, release information, checksums, and malware-scan receipts. Update distributions contain only the matching application payload and update metadata so they do not overwrite user data.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
TLOHome/\line   apps/\line     Windows/\line       tlo-ggi.exe\line       tlo-gi.exe\line       tlo-tag.exe\line       tlo-gsi.exe\line       search-artist-db.exe\line       _internal/              Windows onedir package only\line     macOS/\line       tlo-ggi\line       tlo-gi\line       tlo-tag\line       tlo-gsi\line       search-artist-db\line     Linux/\line       tlo-ggi\line       tlo-gi\line       tlo-tag\line       tlo-gsi\line       search-artist-db\line   TLO_DBs/\line     artists.sqlite\line     venues.txt\line   debug/  dups/  logs/  readyForXfer/  setlists/  staged/\line   README_FIRST.txt\line   TLO-FAQ.txt\line   TLO_Inventory_User_Manual_v351.rtf\line   toBeInventoried.txt}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Every complete distribution includes tlo-gsi, search-artist-db, TLO_DBs/artists.sqlite, and TLO_DBs/venues.txt. The generic Linux applications are also used under WSL. The Windows onedir package places all five executables directly in apps/Windows with one shared apps/Windows/_internal folder; keep that folder with the executables and replace the whole apps/Windows folder when switching between onefile and onedir layouts.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx9396\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Do not run inside the ZIP: Always extract the installation ZIP first. Windows and Linux cannot reliably execute the apps while dependencies, databases, or shell scripts are still compressed.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
3. Pre-installation checklist}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Choose the final TLOHome folder. Use a short absolute path such as C:\\TLOHome on Windows or $HOME/TLOHome on WSL/Linux.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Confirm that TLOHome is writable by the account that will run the apps.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Know how attached drives will be mounted. Windows runs can use drive-letter paths such as E:\\Music. WSL/Linux runs can use paths such as /mnt/e/Music after the drive is mounted and visible to that environment.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Use visible and unique volume names for search roots. They are strongly recommended, especially with external drives, backup drives, WSL paths, or drives that may get different letters over time.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- If setlist.fm lookup will be used, obtain a setlist.fm API key and set SETLISTFM_API_KEY before enabling setlist.fm lookup.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx9396\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Installation contents: The installation ZIP installs the application files and support folders under TLOHome. Pre-installation setup is limited to choosing a writable TLOHome location, preparing environment variables, and making sure mounted drives will be visible.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
4. Windows installation and shortcuts}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Install or refresh TLOHome}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
1.\tab Create or choose the TLOHome folder, for example C:\\TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
2.\tab Extract the installation ZIP so the apps and support folders appear inside TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
3.\tab Confirm that C:\\TLOHome\\apps\\Windows contains tlo-ggi.exe, tlo-gi.exe, tlo-tag.exe, tlo-gsi.exe, and search-artist-db.exe.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
4.\tab Set the TLOHome environment variable and optional variables described in Section 6.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
5.\tab Open a new Windows terminal or restart any already-open TLO app so the changed environment is visible.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
PowerShell example:\line Expand-Archive .\\TLO_V1.2Build351_complete_Windows.zip -DestinationPath C:\\TLOHome\line setx TLOHome "C:\\TLOHome"\line setx TLOCurrentStorage "Backup-1"\line setx SETLISTFM_API_KEY "your-api-key-if-used"}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Optional: pin and edit the Search app shortcut}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx9396\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Shortcut arguments: After the Start Menu shortcut exists, its Target field can include arguments after the EXE path, such as --TLOHome C:\\TLOHome or --find "search text" for the included Search app.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
1.\tab After extracting the distribution, open File Explorer and go to C:\\TLOHome\\apps\\Windows.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
2.\tab Right-click tlo-gsi.exe and choose Pin to Start.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
3.\tab Open the Start menu, right-click the TLO Search item for tlo-gsi.exe, choose More, then choose Open file location.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
4.\tab In the Start Menu shortcut folder that opens, right-click the TLO Search shortcut and choose Properties.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
5.\tab On the Shortcut tab, confirm the Target and set Start in to C:\\TLOHome\\apps\\Windows.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
6.\tab Click the Shortcut key field, press Ctrl+Shift+C, and click OK.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
7.\tab Test the shortcut. Repeat the same pin-to-Start steps for tlo-ggi.exe if you also want the main GUI on Start.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
